                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91a12b2c-6e0b-377a-800f-05810a15298f",
                                        "entry_id": "5dd08d9c-3a4b-3956-a248-864a908312ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A post on the Bluesky social media platform."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b829d101-bfff-41cb-8234-16abe4015e75",
                                                "sense_id": "91a12b2c-6e0b-377a-800f-05810a15298f",
                                                "text": "Bluesky’s users appear to be having fun with the app’s similarities to Twitter, including calling posts on the app “skeets,” as a play on tweets. Not even a plea from Ms. Graber on Thursday to change that name seems to have deterred them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43f0cd4d-1cd3-46e3-b807-9c22331cf592",
                                                "sense_id": "91a12b2c-6e0b-377a-800f-05810a15298f",
                                                "text": "At first, it was kind of fun when Bluesky broke.[…] When threading broke – causing people to receive tonnes of notifications if they replied to a long enough chain of skeets – users created the \"hellthread\", an infinitely long, chaotic conversation"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9693f26c-3f81-44a7-a41e-20ebdcddfd77",
                                                "sense_id": "91a12b2c-6e0b-377a-800f-05810a15298f",
                                                "text": "My last ‘toot’, as Mastodon’s users call tweets, was in December. I’ve never even done a ‘skeet’, the unfortunate name of the Bluesky version."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "334a5e4e-042d-405d-ba74-9936916f4c57",
                                                "sense_id": "91a12b2c-6e0b-377a-800f-05810a15298f",
                                                "text": "Bluesky’s faithful have playfully dubbed posts “skeets” in contrast to tweets – although Bluesky’s own CEO Jay Graber has begged users to stop using that term."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be653732-9e81-45ac-a739-fa1741411765",
                                                "sense_id": "91a12b2c-6e0b-377a-800f-05810a15298f",
                                                "text": "Another skeet! Blue Sky^([sic]) is clearly taking off – not content with picking up a million new accounts on Friday, and another million on Saturday, it has now played its part in two posts on the OBO."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "skeet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f09c9ea-9d44-307a-a608-b5625fa18dcf",
                                        "entry_id": "c43c5a21-60f8-3bcd-9700-a96ccf0bd01b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To create a skeet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90c94dda-5652-4197-9cee-82edfe06fcb4",
                                                "sense_id": "7f09c9ea-9d44-307a-a608-b5625fa18dcf",
                                                "text": "Yeah, and there's a new social media app called Blue Sky, and on it, Senator Brian Schatz from Hawaii, Democrat, he just skeeted, quote, the only way to prevent default with a bipartisan majority and 60 in the Senate is a clean anti-default bill."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b79adaf-50fa-4422-8b41-418362c10f03",
                                                "sense_id": "7f09c9ea-9d44-307a-a608-b5625fa18dcf",
                                                "text": "Bluesky is a bit like the retro Twitter, same colour scheme, similar way of building content etc, and so it reminds people of early Twitter. I am not sure if that’s enough to make people fall in love with Bluesky and go skeeting all day."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
